# Local configuration and device secrets ARE committed (2026-11-17).
# This repository is the private master copy of the exhibit: a fresh clone on
# another laptop must run exactly as this one was left.  Nothing here is a
# shared credential — it is one private board and one laptop.  Do not publish
# this repository.
.env.*
!.env.example
!uc/include/village/secrets.example.h
*.pem
*.key

# AI models.
#   models/piper/        committed — Sara's voice is the project (293 MB)
#   models/waste*/       committed — the classifier must run on a fresh clone
#   models/whisper/      the server binary is committed; the WEIGHTS are not,
#                        because GitHub refuses any file over 100 MB and they
#                        are 142 MB / 466 MB / 1.6 GB.  scripts/download_models.sh
#                        fetches them, and docs/backup.md explains the rest.
models/*
!models/README.md
!models/.gitkeep
!models/piper/
!models/piper/**
!models/waste/
!models/waste/**
!models/waste-resnet50/
!models/waste-resnet50/**
!models/whisper/
!models/whisper/whisper-server

web/frontend/public/audio/*.wav
web/frontend/public/audio/*.mp3
web/frontend/public/audio/*.m4a
web/frontend/public/audio/*.ogg
recordings/
*.raw

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# Node / build outputs
node_modules/
web/frontend/dist/
web/frontend/.vite/
web/frontend/coverage/
playwright-report/
test-results/
*.tsbuildinfo

# PlatformIO / firmware build outputs
uc/.pio/
uc/.pioenvs/
uc/.piolibdeps/
uc/.vscode/
*.bin
*.elf
*.map

# Runtime data.  `data/village.db` and `data/waste-samples/` are committed on
# purpose (see the end of this file): the database is the village's own state
# and the photos are the only copy of what the classifier got wrong.  Caches,
# logs, PID files and the rolling crop log are not.
data/*
run/
logs/
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
server.log

# Scratch / editor / OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*.swo
/tmp/

# --- Committed on purpose -----------------------------------------------------
# Last rules win, so these undo the runtime-data block above.
!data/village.db
!data/waste-samples/
!data/waste-samples/**
!data/waste-corrections.jsonl
# …and these undo the firmware's `*.bin` rule, which would otherwise swallow the
# MobileNet weights (`models/waste/weights.bin`).
!models/waste/**
!models/waste-resnet50/**
